# Astatine · At · gate 85

**Astatine** (At) is element **85** of the periodic table — a **halogen**, period 6, group 17, p-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **[210] (most stable isotope)**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
The rarest naturally occurring element on Earth — less than a gram exists at any moment.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **85** falls on **0:1 — first valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **0**. That state is *the first reach of emptiness toward one — potential, charge, the rising edge* — the nature of emergence here is **electrical**. Astatine is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — electrical
This emergent carries the **electrical** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#3fd0e0`.

